   "source": [
    "### Example 2: misscalibration of ar(p)-garch(p,q) models\n",
    "One can extend the example of the simple ar(1) models to a broader class of models. For instance\n",
    "\\begin{equation*}\n",
    "    Y:=y_t|\\mathcal{F}_{t-1} \\sim \\mathcal{N}(\\mu_t(\\boldsymbol{y_{t-1}}),\\sigma^2_t(\\varepsilon_{t-1},\\sigma^2_{t-1})).\n",
    "\\end{equation*}\n",
    "with the ARMA(p,q)-GARCH(p,q) process as a prime example. It is  well known how to estimate these types of models. While estimation of these models is well understood, it is much more challenging to detect changes in the underlying data-generating process. For example, parameter values may shift at unknown discrete time points, or the model order itself may vary over time. In such cases, sequential tests offer a practical approach to determine whether the current model is becoming redundant and should be updated or replaced."
   ]
