    "## Non parametric setting\n",
    "---\n",
    "In the non-parametric setting, the paper suggest testing the null against the kernel density\n",
    "\\begin{equation*}\n",
    "    E^{K,b,\\zeta^{k}}(Z_F) = \\sum_{i=1}^{k} \\frac{1}{b}K(\\frac{Z_F-\\zeta_i}{b}).\n",
    "\\end{equation*}\n",
    "Here $K(\\cdot)$ is the kernel and $b$ is the bandwidth. Similar to the MLE setting the kernel and bandwidth can be taken sequentially and the paper uses the boundary corrected Epanechnikov kernel.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "@Jako boundary corrected kernel estimation doesnt exist in python so I have to manually implement this at a later time."
   ]
